  "blocks": {
    "\"No, write it up as a spec — break it into tickets, run each one in its own session. Trying to do the whole thing in a single context will hit the dumb zone before you're halfway.\"": "“不，把它写成规格说明——拆成多个任务，每个任务在自己的会话中执行。如果试图在单一上下文里完成全部工作，还没做到一半就会进入<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/smart-zone\">迟钝区</a>。”",
    "\"Should this all be one session?\"": "“这些工作都应该放在一次会话里完成吗？”",
    "A handoff artifact describing a multi-session piece of work — what's being built, not how each session does its share. Mutates as work progresses. Made of tickets.": "规格说明是一种<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/handoff-artifact\">交接产物</a>，用于描述一项跨多个<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>的工作：说明要构建什么，而不是每次会话具体怎样完成自己的部分。它会随着工作推进持续变化，并由多个<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/ticket\">任务</a>组成。",
    "Specs come in recognisable styles, mostly inherited from how teams already write things down. A product requirements document (PRD) leans toward the user-facing what and why — features, behaviour, acceptance criteria. A design doc or RFC leans technical — the chosen approach, the alternatives rejected, the trade-offs. At the small end, a plain plan.md with a checklist of tickets does the same job for a multi-session feature. The style matters less than the role: for the agent, each of these is the same thing — the durable statement of intent it reads at the start of every session.": "规格说明有一些常见形式，大多沿用团队原有的记录方式。产品需求文档（PRD）更偏向用户视角的“做什么”和“为什么”——功能、行为和验收标准；设计文档或 RFC 更偏技术——选定的方案、被否决的备选方案以及其中权衡。规模较小时，一份带任务检查清单的普通 <code>plan.md</code>，也能为跨会话功能完成同样工作。形式不如角色重要：对<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>而言，它们都是同一类东西——一份持久的意图声明，每次会话开始时都会读取。",
    "The spec exists because sessions are disposable and big work isn't. Anything that takes more than one context window of effort needs a home outside the context — somewhere in the agent's environment that survives clearing, whether that's a file in the repo, a GitHub issue, or an issue tracker the agent can reach. The spec is that home: the goal, the constraints, the decisions made so far, and the list of tickets with their status. Any fresh session can read it and know where the work stands without inheriting the previous session's accumulated noise.": "规格说明之所以存在，是因为会话可以随时丢弃，大型工作却不能。凡是需要超过一个<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>才能完成的任务，都需要在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context\">上下文</a>之外拥有一个长期载体——位于<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/environment\">智能体环境</a>中，能够在<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/clearing\">清空</a>后继续存在；它可以是仓库中的文件、GitHub issue，或智能体能够访问的任务跟踪器。规格说明就是这个载体：其中记录目标、约束、截至当前作出的决策，以及任务列表和各自状态。任何全新会话都能读取它，立即了解工作进展，而无需继承上一会话累积的噪声。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
  },
